{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require food labels to disclose painful procedures done without pain relief",
        "additional_details": "Switzerland's law covers farming procedures but not slaughter. The UK already tracks stunning methods used at every abattoir through FSA surveys - this data already exists. We ask Government to require it on the label: how an animal was killed, whether it was rendered unconscious first, and whether it received any pain relief - for every method, not just some, so shoppers see the full truth and not part of it.",
        "background": "Switzerland requires food labels to state when animals underwent painful procedures - such as castration or dehorning - without pain relief. We ask the UK Government to introduce similar mandatory labelling for meat, milk and dairy, so shoppers can make an informed choice.",
